      </div>
      <div type="apparatus">
      <listApp>
        <app loc="16" ana="#app.expunged"><lem>ⲡⲙⲩⲥⲧⲏ <gap reason="illegible" quantity="4" unit="character"/></lem><note>expunged with dots: a dittography from l. 18 caused by homoioteleuton</note></app>
        <app loc="28" ana="#app.confirmation"><lem><supplied reason="lost">ⲁⲣⲧⲁ</supplied>ⲝⲟⲟⲥ</lem><note>at the beginning of the line, apparently so</note></app>
        <app loc="28" ana="#app.rejected"><rdg resp="#edition">ⲁⲣⲧⲁⲝⲁⲣⲏⲥ</rdg><note>in any case not the expected form</note></app>
        <app loc="34" ana="#app.traces-report"><lem>ⲉϥ</lem><rdg resp="#edition">ⲛⲉϥ</rdg><rdg resp="#edition"><supplied reason="lost">ⲛⲉ</supplied>ⲙⲉϥ</rdg><note>before ⲉϥ traces of ⲛ̣ or ⲙ̣</note></app>
      </listApp>
      </div>
      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1" ana="#tr.print">The framed manuscript page number [ⲓⲉ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="14" ana="#tr.bracket">The edition prints [ⲟⲥ ⲁⲧ(ⲣ)ⲟⲩ]: the ⲣ stands in parentheses inside the restoration. The parentheses cannot be encoded; the restoration is recorded as [ⲟⲥ ⲁⲧⲣⲟⲩ].</p>
        <p n="16" ana="#tr.bracket">The edition prints the words from ⲡⲙⲩⲥⲧⲏⲣⲓⲟⲛ to the line end in double square brackets (deletion by the scribe); encoded as ⟦ ⟧ (del rend=expunction).</p>
        <p n="20" ana="#tr.print">Measured overline 1127–1198: it covers ⲣⲕⲗⲥ and not the preceding ⲡ.</p>
      </div>
